{"availability":"available","full":"HerRei/tsp_aco_gui","name":"tsp_aco_gui","description":"Java Swing GUI for visualizing Ant Colony Optimization on the Traveling Salesman Problem, with random and NYC datasets, adjustable ACO parameters, live tours, and a GitHub Pages demo.","category":"Other","language":"Java","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-23T22:48:44Z","updated":"2026-05-07T15:04:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://herrei.github.io/tsp_aco_gui/","topics":["aco","heuristic-search-algorithms","maven","meta-heuristic","optimisation","swing-gui","tsp-solver"],"demo":"https://herrei.github.io/tsp_aco_gui/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:03.011Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:03.011Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:03.011Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:18:03.011Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This was a small project for a final assignment, at Unibasel. It was about Meta-Heuristic Algorithms. I built this to have a tool to experiment and show my findings. Most of the online tools i found for ACO were very performance constraint so this was the main point of concern.","Note about the GitHub Pages demo: GitHub Pages cannot run the Java Swing app directly in the browser. The JavaScript in docs/demo.js is not an exact copy of the Java source, but a small browser implementation of the same ACO/TSP ideas so the project can be tried online. The main implementation is still the Java code in src/main/java/."],"features":["Random dataset: generate N cities and solve/visualize the TSP tour.","NYC dataset: fixed landmarks + optional nycmap.png background.","Live visualization: shows current ant tours (semi-transparent) and the best tour found so far.","Adjustable parameters: ants, iterations, alpha, beta, rho (evaporation), Q, and animation delay.","Road block demo (NYC only): toggle a single blocked edge to see how it affects solutions."